{"text": " Yo, what's up? How's everyone doing today? First off, welcome to the hackathon. Super excited to see everyone here and huge shout out to Sunday for bringing us all together. So today is all about building something cool, experimenting with new ideas, and honestly just having fun with it. The theme for today's hackathon is 3D simulations on the web using tools like 3.js and AI. And the idea is pretty simple. Think about something that happens in the real world, figure out how it works, and bring it to life in your browser. Maybe you want to simulate traffic in Boston, create a crazy weather system, build a solar system, or have a thousand particles flying around your screen. Whatever it is, you get to be creative with it. And here's the cool part. With AI coding tools, you don't have to spend hours figuring out all the complicated physics and math. You can focus more on your ideas and actually making them happen. Also, don't worry if you've never worked with 3D before. That's totally fine. This is a place to learn, try new things, meet cool people, and maybe even build something you didn't think you could build. And one thing I really want to emphasize is don't overthink it. You don't need to build the most complicated project in the room. Start with something simple, make it interactive, and see where it goes. Talk to the people around you, share ideas, ask questions, and don't be afraid to experiment. By the end of today, hopefully everyone walks away with something cool they've built, something new they've learned, and maybe a few new friends. So yeah, that's pretty much it. Huge thanks again to Sunday for bringing us all together. And I'll see you next time. Thanks to Sunday and to all of you for showing up. I'm really excited to see what everyone comes up with.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.14, "text": " Yo, what's up? How's everyone doing today? First off, welcome to the hackathon. Super excited to", "tokens": [50365, 761